{"schema": 2, "id": "religion-coptic", "title": "Coptic", "label": "Coptic", "description": "", "extract": "Le Coptic est un paquebot-mixte de la White Star Line mis en service en 1881. Jumeau de l'Arabic, il est construit par les chantiers Harland & Wolff pour être affrété sur la ligne du Pacifique par l'Occidental and Oriental Steamship Company (O&O); il effectue cependant sa traversée inaugurale sur la ligne de l'Atlantique Nord avant de partir pour celle de Hong Kong à San Francisco en 1882.", "type": "religion", "typeLabel": "Religion", "continents": ["Afrique", "Asie", "Europe"], "epochs": ["antiquite", "moyen-age", "moderne", "contemporain"], "from": 452, "to": 2000, "itemCount": 59, "items": ["Adana", "Agew", "Aksum", "Al Gharbia", "Al Watah", "Alexandria", "Angot", "Ankober", "Armenia", "Asosa", "Asyut", "Asyut South", "Awsa", "Berber", "Borena", "Butana", "Cairo", "Damot", "Dar Ja'al", "Delta", "Dembiya", "Diamientia", "Djado", "Dongola", "Erserum", "Erzincan", "Gezira", "Gojjam", "Gonder", "Halaib", "Hamasien", "Ibrim", "Illubabor", "Kargah", "Kefa", "Lasta", "Massawa", "Melikates", "Mendefera", "Minya"], "source": "https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coptic", "articleLicense": "CC BY-SA 4.0", "image": "", "imageCredit": {"filename": "StateLibQld_1_126227_Coptic_(ship).jpg", "artist": "Contributeur Wikimedia Commons", "license": "Public domain", "licenseUrl": "", "credit": "Item is held by John Oxley Library, State Library of Queensland.", "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:StateLibQld_1_126227_Coptic_(ship).jpg"}, "revision": "", "sha256": "09681c8e620b729f928d424cbeb2f73dea06529a822c10933c3dcbd339e65d08"}